(350, 'exec', 'const patch = "*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /work/verification.k\\n@@\\n endmodule\\n+\\n+// This module promotes the separately proved loop claim to a rewrite lemma\\n+// for the end-to-end proof.  prove.sh first closes the same statement as a\\n+// claim against SUM-PRODUCT-VERIFICATION, then compiles this staging module.\\n+module SUM-PRODUCT-LEMMA\\n+  imports SUM-PRODUCT-VERIFICATION\\n+\\n+  rule\\n+    <k>\\n+      #loop(list(intVals(IS)), Name(\\"number\\"), sumProductLoopBody)\\n+      => .K\\n+    </k>\\n+    <env> 1 </env>\\n+    <scopes>\\n+      -1 |-> builtinsScope\\n+      0 |-> scope(GLOBAL:Map, parent(-1))\\n+      1 |-> scope(\\n+        \\"numbers\\" |-> INPUT:Val\\n+        \\"total\\" |-> SUM:Int\\n+        \\"product\\" |-> PRODUCT:Int\\n+        \\"number\\" |-> CURRENT:Int,\\n+        parent(0))\\n+      =>\\n+      -1 |-> builtinsScope\\n+      0 |-> scope(GLOBAL, parent(-1))\\n+      1 |-> scope(\\n+        \\"numbers\\" |-> INPUT\\n+        \\"total\\" |-> intSeqSumFrom(SUM, IS)\\n+        \\"product\\" |-> intSeqProductFrom(PRODUCT, IS)\\n+        \\"number\\" |-> lastInt(IS, CURRENT),\\n+        parent(0))\\n+    </scopes>\\n+    [priority(40)]\\n+endmodule\\n*** Update File: /work/spec.k\\n@@\\n-module SUM-PRODUCT-SPEC\\n+module SUM-PRODUCT-LOOP-SPEC\\n@@\\n-  // End-to-end theorem over the exact translated module and an arbitrary\\n-  // finite sequence of mathematical integers.\\n+endmodule\\n+\\n+module SUM-PRODUCT-FUNCTION-SPEC\\n+  imports SUM-PRODUCT-LEMMA\\n+\\n+  // End-to-end theorem over the exact translated module and an arbitrary\\n+  // finite sequence of mathematical integers.  SUM-PRODUCT-LEMMA is the\\n+  // staged rewrite form of loop-correct, which prove.sh proves first.\\n@@\\n endmodule\\n*** End Patch";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n')
